@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito66-nouns`
IMPORT `ito66-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- s 66(d) and (e).  Lines 2479-2484.
--
--   (ד)(1) הוראות סעיף קטן (א) יחולו לגבי בני זוג שיש להם מקור הכנסה משותף,
--          רק אם התקיימו כל אלה:
--     (א) יגיעתו האישית של כל אחד מבני הזוג נדרשת לייצור ההכנסה ממקור
--         ההכנסה המשותף;
--     (ב) כל אחד מבני הזוג מקבל הכנסה התואמת את תרומתו לייצור ההכנסה ממקור
--         ההכנסה המשותף ועומדת ביחס ישיר לתרומתו לייצור ההכנסה כאמור;
--     (ג) אם ההכנסה מופקת בבית המגורים של בני הזוג – בית המגורים משמש, דרך
--         קבע, את מקור ההכנסה המשותף ומרבית פעילות מקור ההכנסה האמור נעשית
--         בבית המגורים;
--   (2) לעניין סעיף קטן זה, ”מקור הכנסה משותף“ – מקור הכנסה של בן זוג התלוי
--       במקור ההכנסה של בן הזוג השני.
--   (ה) (בוטל).
--
-- (d) is placed before (a) in this row because (a) cannot be applied without
-- it: it is the gate on the whole of subsection (a).
--
-- (d)(2), the definition, is not computed: whether one spouse's source of
-- income depends on the other's is a fact the caller supplies, as the MAYBE
-- field `common source of income` on `Spouses in a tax year`.
--
-- READING (fork F1 in NOTES.md).  (d)(1) says subsection (a) applies "to
-- spouses who have a common source of income" only if all three conditions
-- hold.  Taken literally, as here, the gate is on the COUPLE: where the
-- conditions fail, subsection (a) does not apply to them at all.  The other
-- reading puts the gate on the INCOME from the common source alone, and s
-- 64B(b) (line 2441) speaks that way: "הכנסה ממקור הכנסה משותף לפי סעיף 66(ד)
-- שלא מתקיימות לגביה הוראות אותו סעיף".
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 66(d) — spouses with a common source of income`

@ref s 66(d)(1)(b), line 2481
GIVEN `the source` IS A `A common source of income`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(d)(1)(b) — each spouse is paid according to his contribution, from` `the source` MEANS
        `the source`'s `each spouse receives income matching his contribution to producing it`
    AND `the source`'s `each spouse's income stands in direct proportion to his contribution`

-- A proviso limb: it bites only where the income is produced in the residence.
@ref s 66(d)(1)(c), line 2482
GIVEN `the source` IS A `A common source of income`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(d)(1)(c) — if produced in the residence, the residence is the permanent seat of` `the source` MEANS
        NOT `the source`'s `produced in the spouses' residence`
    OR  (    `the source`'s `the residence serves the common source permanently`
         AND `the source`'s `most of the activity of the source is carried on in the residence`)

@ref s 66(d)(1)(a)-(c), lines 2480-2482
GIVEN `the source` IS A `A common source of income`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(d)(1) — every condition is met by` `the source` MEANS
        "(a)" ... `the source`'s `the personal exertion of each spouse is required to produce the income`
    ... "(b)" ... `s 66(d)(1)(b) — each spouse is paid according to his contribution, from` `the source`
    AND "(c)" ... `s 66(d)(1)(c) — if produced in the residence, the residence is the permanent seat of` `the source`

-- Spouses with no common source are outside (d)(1); spouses whose common
-- source meets every condition pass it.  Either way (a) applies to them on its
-- own terms, under every reading of fork F1.
@ref s 66(d)(1) chapeau, line 2479
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(d)(1) — the spouses have no common source of income, or one that meets every condition:` couple MEANS
    CONSIDER couple's `common source of income`
    WHEN NOTHING       THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST `source` THEN `s 66(d)(1) — every condition is met by` `source`

-- FORK F1 (version 0.4.0; RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08, SHRUG; inventory 02-F1).
-- Where a common source fails (d)(1), "הוראות סעיף קטן (א) יחולו לגבי בני זוג
-- שיש להם מקור הכנסה משותף, רק אם התקיימו כל אלה" names the spouses, so (i)
-- subsection (a) does not apply to them at all (the reading of 0.1.0-0.3.0);
-- but s 64B(b), line 2441, speaks of "הכנסה ממקור הכנסה משותף לפי סעיף 66(ד)
-- שלא מתקיימות לגביה הוראות אותו סעיף", so (ii) only the income from the
-- common source is kept out of (a).  The default declines where the two give
-- different answers; the rules that ask it say where that is.
@ref s 66(d)(1), line 2479; s 64B(b), line 2441; fork F1; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of section 66(d)(1) where a common source of income fails its conditions`
`section 66(d)(1) — the reading this row takes where a common source of income fails its conditions` MEANS
    `declined where the readings of section 66(d)(1) differ`

@ref s 66(d)(1), line 2479; s 64B(b), line 2441; fork F1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 66(d)(1) does not say whether a common source of income that fails its conditions keeps subsection (a) from the spouses or only from the income of that source` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 66(d)(1) does not say whether a common source of income that fails its conditions keeps subsection (a) from the spouses or only from the income of that source"

-- Reading (ii) needs to know how much of the income of the spouse who is not
-- the registered spouse comes from the source; where the facts do not say,
-- it cannot answer.
@ref s 66(d)(1), line 2479; fork F1, reading (ii)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the facts do not say how much of the income from personal exertion of the spouse who is not the registered spouse comes from the common source of income` MEANS
    REFUSE "the facts do not say how much of the income from personal exertion of the spouse who is not the registered spouse comes from the common source of income"

-- The reading of F1 a couple asks for, or this row's switch.
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A `A reading of section 66(d)(1) where a common source of income fails its conditions`
`the reading of section 66(d)(1) taken for` couple MEANS
    CONSIDER couple's `the readings of section 66 to take, if not this row's`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN `section 66(d)(1) — the reading this row takes where a common source of income fails its conditions`
    WHEN JUST rs THEN rs's `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`

-- The gate itself.
-- Version 0.2.0 (02-V4): it takes the couple, and so the tax year, and
-- refuses a year the deposited text does not govern (A1).
-- Version 0.4.0 (F1): where a common source fails (d)(1), reading (i) answers
-- FALSE; reading (ii) answers TRUE, (a) applying to the spouses save the
-- income of that source, which `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the
-- registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` and the assembly
-- keep out; and as the two always differ there, the default declines.
@ref s 66(d)(1) chapeau, line 2479; s 66 amendment list, line 2454; fork F1
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(d) — subsection (a) applies to` couple MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (IF   `s 66(d)(1) — the spouses have no common source of income, or one that meets every condition:` couple
         THEN TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the reading of section 66(d)(1) taken for` couple
              WHEN `subsection (a) does not apply to the spouses at all`                      THEN FALSE
              WHEN `subsection (a) does not apply to the income from the common source alone` THEN TRUE
              WHEN `declined where the readings of section 66(d)(1) differ`
                  THEN `section 66(d)(1) does not say whether a common source of income that fails its conditions keeps subsection (a) from the spouses or only from the income of that source`)

-- Whether the facts give that income, for a common source that fails (d)(1).
@ref s 66(d)(1), line 2479; fork F1, reading (ii)
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(d)(1) — the facts give the income of the spouse who is not the registered spouse from a common source that fails, for` couple MEANS
    CONSIDER couple's `common source of income`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST `source` THEN
        CONSIDER `source`'s `the income from personal exertion it gives the spouse who is not the registered spouse, if known`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 66(d)(1) — every condition is met by` `source`
        WHEN JUST x  THEN TRUE

-- Fork F1, reading (ii): the income of the spouse who is not the registered
-- spouse from a common source that fails (d)(1), as the facts give it.  0
-- where the source passes or there is none.
@ref s 66(d)(1), line 2479; fork F1, reading (ii)
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(d)(1) — the income from personal exertion of the spouse who is not the registered spouse from a common source that fails, for` couple MEANS
    CONSIDER couple's `common source of income`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
    WHEN JUST `source` THEN
        IF   `s 66(d)(1) — every condition is met by` `source`
        THEN 0
        ELSE CONSIDER `source`'s `the income from personal exertion it gives the spouse who is not the registered spouse, if known`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN `the facts do not say how much of the income from personal exertion of the spouse who is not the registered spouse comes from the common source of income`
             WHEN JUST x  THEN x

§ `Section 66(e) — repealed`

-- Line 2484: "{{ח:תת|(ה)}} {{ח:הערה|(בוטל).}}".  A stub so the section has no
-- silent gap; no operative content.
GIVETH A STRING
`s 66(e) — repealed` MEANS "(בוטל)"
